Hi @nicoespeon 

Here is a new refactoring proposal: Change function signature.

At the moment we are able to change "parameters arguments" of a function.

Cases:

- Given a function with two parameters:

```javascript
function add(param: number, num2: number) {
  return param + num2;
}

add(1, 200);
```
- Expect to change parameters and arguments orders

```javascript
function add(num2: number, param: number) {
  return param + num2;
}

add(200, 1);
``` 


![function-arguments-change](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8685132/194755839-5097690a-2609-4aab-9381-48cb4dee5eed.gif)



> Question: Why "Change Signature" open a Tab for order definition?
> Answer: I not able to create a "Popup" for asking orders. vscode does not contain a (at the momento) API to give us that functionality. So I render a "Webview" as a sidebar. I found that [Color Picker](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=anseki.vscode-color) has a Popup but I don't want to look how they created it (lazy boy :P)

- Given a function with second param as optional
```javascript
function add(paramRequired, paramOptional: number = 1) {
  return paramRequired + paramOptional;
}

add(200);
```
- Expect to put `undefined` as a value when there are no value in call expression

```javascript
function add(paramOptional: number = 1, paramRequired) {
  return paramRequired + paramOptional;
}

add(undefined, 200);
```

There are more cases in test case.

- Given a function with value and callback
```javascript
function repeat(f, n) {
  return Array(n)
    .fill(null)
    .map((_, i) => f(i));
}

const squares = repeat((i) => i * i, 5);
```
- Expect to change argument order even if there a callback
```javascript
function repeat(n, f) {
  return Array(n)
    .fill(null)
    .map((_, i) => f(i));
}

const squares = repeat(5, (i) => i * i);
```


### What about modules

I develop the funcionality to search (using vscode Find References) references in base code and change arguments orders based on user definition

![modules](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8685132/194756418-5f9b5187-79f8-42d8-a7ea-c64713ddb30b.gif)

### To Fix

For modules imported with aliases would not found a references and the changes will break app -> need to look how to prevent changes when there are aliases for a exported funcion

### Next?

Maybe we can add functionalities like:
- Remove param
- Add new param with a value or default value
Feedback are welcome :)

